CONCLUSION: PARI's Jacobian/divisor arithmetic is restricted to genus<=2 (hyperell*).
A genus-5 NON-hyperelliptic curve has no Mumford representation and no Abel-Jacobi in PARI.

=== V_q non-hyperelliptic ===
V_q = 3 quadrics in P^4: a smooth complete intersection curve of genus 5.
Its Jacobian splits as a product of FIVE elliptic curves (J ~ E^5), so dim J = 5 = g.
A hyperelliptic genus-5 curve has a 2:1 map to P^1 and its Jacobian does NOT split into
5 elliptic factors over Q with this (Z/2)^3 character structure. The (Z/2)^3 quotient
structure (3 conic quotients of genus 0, 3 genus-1, 1 genus-2->2xE) is the signature of
a bielliptic/multi-elliptic NON-hyperelliptic curve. (Same conclusion stated in
QUADRATIC-CHABAUTY-RANK3.md: 'V_q is not hyperelliptic'.)

